{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show --format=fuller 4295681 -- packages/axylo/src && sed -n '105,148p' docs/02-product-spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"commit 4295681125dfc5ffe2e6ecc60478103d4e2158d1\nAuthor:     canarit <gaqu1994@gmail.com>\nAuthorDate: Thu Nov 19 08:47:22 2026 +0100\nCommit:     canarit <gaqu1994@gmail.com>\nCommitDate: Thu Nov 19 08:47:22 2026 +0100\n\n    The plot's keyboard instructions follow the chart: zoom keys only where zoom exists, series keys only with several series, slices on a donut (Codex gpt-6.2-sol xhigh)\n    \n    Found by the Phase 1 rerun: category bars and donuts told readers about zoom\n    keys they do not have. Three optional message keys (donutInstructions,\n    seriesInstructions, zoomInstructions); an existing plotInstructions override\n    stays whole.\n    \n    Coordinator: type check clean; plot-description and A6-A10 browser tests 57\n    pass; chart + a11y 323 pass. Size: everything 116.12 KiB, 118 bytes over the\n    116 KiB target (line only 97.17 of 98); a trim follows.\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts b/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts\nindex deedcbd..20c6b9b 100644\n--- a/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts\n+++ b/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ import type {\n   Rect, ResolvedTheme, StepDirection, TooltipModel, View, XValue,\n } from '../core/contracts';\n import type { Messages } from '../public';\n-import { fill } from '../messages';\n+import { defaultMessages, fill, messageLanguage } from '../messages';\n import {\n   overlayWith, OUTLINE_REACH, RING_REACH, RING_STROKE, alignedRows, canZoomIn, datumReading, minimumWidth, panWindow,\n   pinchWidth, pixelOf, positionAt, rangeWindow, refsAt, ringRect, sameRef, stepAcross, zoomStep, targetBox, targetOf, valueText, PAN_SHARE, ZOOM_FACTOR,\n@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ import { sliceText } from '../lookup/text';\n import { barPattern } from '../scene/bars';\n import { readPosition } from '../reader/x';\n import { printedX } from '../reader/table';\n-import { activeElementOf, placeChildren, setAttr, make, keepFocusOnPress, hideFromAT } from './attributes';\n+import { activeElementOf, placeChildren, setAttr, setText, make, keepFocusOnPress, hideFromAT } from './attributes';\n import { mappingOf, rectToViewport, toLocal, toViewport, visibleRegion, type Point } from './mapping';\n import { insideCorridor, intersect, type PlacementInput } from './placement';\n import { identityOf, matchesIdentity, sameTarget, type Identity } from './pointer';\n@@ -116,6 +116,51 @@ export interface Committed extends ControlsState {\n   readonly pixelRatio: number;\n }\n \n+type InstructionKey = 'plotInstructions' | 'donutInstructions' | 'seriesInstructions' | 'zoomInstructions';\n+\n+function offersZoom(d: ControlsState): d is ControlsState & {\n+  readonly zoom: true | 'touch'; readonly tooSmall: false; readonly view: Exclude<View, { kind: 'donut' }>;\n+} {\n+  return d.zoom !== false && !d.tooSmall && d.view.kind !== 'donut';\n+}\n+\n+// The guard names a subtype, so a failed check narrows only away from null, never to `never`.\n+function plotReady(d: Committed | null): d is Committed & { readonly ready: true } {\n+  return d !== null && d.ready && d.layout.kind === 'plot';\n+}\n+\n+/** Some series is shown: with every one hidden by the legend there is nothing to read (new item 8). */\n+function readable(d: Committed): boolean {\n+  return d.view.kind === 'donut' || d.view.visible.some(Boolean);\n+}\n+\n+/** The instructions for the committed plot, with a language for each sentence (spec A2, A10, I3). */\n+export function plotDescription(d: Committed): { text: string; lang: string | null }[] {\n+  if (!d.interactive || !plotReady(d)) return [];\n+  const { messages, view } = d;\n+  const overridden = (key: InstructionKey) => messageLanguage(messages, key) === null;\n+  // A plotInstructions override could already be a complete translation of the old description.\n+  const legacy = overridden('plotInstructions');\n+  const parts: { text: string; lang: string | null }[] = [];\n+  const add = (key: InstructionKey) => {\n+    const text = messages[key] ?? defaultMessages[key];\n+    if (text !== '') parts.push({ text, lang: d.english(key) });\n+  };\n+  if (readable(d) && d.lookup.count > 0) {\n+    if (view.kind === 'donut') {\n+      add(!legacy || overridden('donutInstructions') ? 'donutInstructions' : 'plotInstructions');\n+    } else {\n+      add('plotInstructions');\n+      // Scatter's series keys skip a series with no points in the current window.\n+      const shown = view.visible.filter((on, i) =>\n+        on && (view.kind !== 'scatter' || view.visiblePoints[i]!.end > view.visiblePoints[i]!.start));\n+      if (shown.length > 1 && (!legacy || overridden('seriesInstructions'))) add('seriesInstructions');\n+    }\n+  }\n+  if (offersZoom(d) && (!legacy || overridden('zoomInstructions'))) add('zoomInstructions');\n+  return parts;\n+}\n+\n export interface Actions {\n   /** A window in x positions, or null for everything. Goes through the public `zoom` path. */\n   zoom(window: Span | null): void;\n@@ -613,22 +658,12 @@ export function createInteraction(parts: InteractionParts, figure: Figure, rende\n     return view.kind === 'line' || view.kind === 'area' || view.kind === 'bar';\n   }\n \n-  // The guards name a subtype, so a failed check narrows only away from null, never to `never`.\n-  function plotReady(d: Committed | null): d is Committed & { readonly ready: true } {\n-    return d !== null && d.ready && d.layout.kind === 'plot';\n-  }\n-\n   /** A zoomed window with nothing in it: the plot keeps its focus and its zoom keys, so the reader can go back. */\n   function recoverable<T extends ControlsState>(d: T | null): d is T & { readonly zoomed: true } {\n     // Loading and error are not an empty window: zooming out would not bring anything back (new item 8).\n     return d !== null && !d.ready && d.empty === true && d.zoom !== false && d.zoomed && !d.tooSmall;\n   }\n \n-  /** Some series is shown: with every one hidden by the legend there is nothing to read (new item 8). */\n-  function readable(d: Committed): boolean {\n-    return d.view.kind === 'donut' || d.view.visible.some(Boolean);\n-  }\n-\n   function firstDatum(d: Committed): DatumRef | null {\n     if (aligned(d.view)) {\n       const x = stepAcross(d.view, null, 'first');\n@@ -1748,9 +1783,9 @@ export function createInteraction(parts: InteractionParts, figure: Figure, rende\n     if (d.ready) items.push(...legendItems(d));\n     // Inside a toolbar marked English, a replaced label is marked with the page's language again.\n     const inherited = d.english('controlsLabel') ? d.pageLang : null;\n-    const button = (key: keyof Messages, activate: () => void, disabled = false): ToolbarItem =>\n+    const button = (key: Exclude<keyof Messages, InstructionKey>, activate: () => void, disabled = false): ToolbarItem =>\n       ({ key, label: m[key], lang: d.english(key) ?? inherited, className: 'axylo-control', activate, disabled });\n-    if (d.zoom && !d.tooSmall && d.view.kind !== 'donut' && (d.ready || recoverable(d))) {\n+    if (offersZoom(d) && (d.ready || recoverable(d))) {\n       const window = d.zoomed ? d.view.xDomain : d.view.xFull;\n       if (d.ready) items.push(button('zoomIn', () => zoomBy(1 / ZOOM_FACTOR), !canZoomIn(d.view, window)));\n       // Where a drag selects a range, two clicks can too (spec I4, WCAG 2.5.7): a toggle.\n@@ -1849,6 +1884,7 @@ export function createInteraction(parts: InteractionParts, figure: Figure, rende\n     if (!usable) handOff();\n     proxy.hidden = !usable;\n     ring.hidden = !usable;\n+    if (instructions) instructions.hidden = !usable;\n     if (!usable) return;\n     const p = d.layout.kind === 'plot' ? d.layout.plot : { x: 0, y: 0, width: d.layout.width, height: d.layout.height };\n     const style = `left: ${p.x}px; top: ${p.y}px; width: ${p.width}px; height: ${p.height}px;`;\n@@ -1863,11 +1899,15 @@ export function createInteraction(parts: InteractionParts, figure: Figure, rende\n     // language, but a form control named only by hidden text fails axe's label-title-only.)\n     const proxyLang = readingLang(d);\n     setAttr(proxy, 'aria-label', d.messages.plotLabel);\n-    // How to move in the plot, as its description (the plotInstructions message).\n     if (instructions) {\n-      if (instructions.textContent !== d.messages.plotInstructions) instructions.textContent = d.messages.plotInstructions;\n-      setAttr(instructions, 'lang', d.english('plotInstructions') ?? (proxyLang ? d.pageLang : null));\n-      setAttr(proxy, 'aria-describedby', instructions.id);\n+      const parts = plotDescription(d);\n+      for (const [i, { text, lang }] of parts.entries()) {\n+        const span = instructions.children[i] ?? instructions.appendChild(doc.createElement('span'));\n+        setText(span, i === 0 ? text : ` ${text}`);\n+        setAttr(span, 'lang', lang ?? (proxyLang ? d.pageLang : null));\n+      }\n+      while (instructions.children.length > parts.length) instructions.lastElementChild!.remove();\n+      setAttr(proxy, 'aria-describedby', parts.length ? instructions.id : null);\n     }\n     const type = { line: 'typeLine', area: 'typeArea', bar: 'typeBar', scatter: 'typeScatter', donut: 'typeDonut' } as const;\n     setAttr(proxy, 'aria-roledescription', fill(d.messages.plotRole, { type: d.messages[type[d.kind]] }));\ndiff --git a/packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts b/packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts\nindex 24edd3c..b407d10 100644\n--- a/packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts\n+++ b/packages/axylo/src/messages/index.ts\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ const chartSummary = '{type} chart with {seriesCount} series. {xLabel} from {xMi\n const fullChartSummary = '{type} chart with {seriesCount} series. {xLabel} from {xMin} to {xMax}. {yLabel} from {yMin} to {yMax}.';\n const donutSlice = '{label}: {value} ({percent}).';\n \n-export const defaultMessages: Messages = {\n+export const defaultMessages: Required<Messages> = {\n   viewAsTable: 'View as table',\n   hideTable: 'Hide table',\n   noData: 'No data',\n@@ -59,7 +59,10 @@ export const defaultMessages: Messages = {\n   panLeft: 'Pan left',\n   panRight: 'Pan right',\n   jumpNotFound: 'No row matches {x}. Example: {example}',\n-  plotInstructions: 'Left and right arrows move between points, up and down between series, and Enter selects. Plus and minus zoom; 0 resets.',\n+  plotInstructions: 'Left and right arrows move between points along x. Enter selects.',\n+  donutInstructions: 'Arrow keys move between slices. Enter selects.',\n+  seriesInstructions: 'Up and down arrows move between series.',\n+  zoomInstructions: 'Plus and minus zoom. Press 0 to reset. Hold Shift with left or right to pan the zoomed view.',\n   selectRange: 'Select range',\n   seeTable: 'See table.',\n   totalMixed: '{positive} and {negative}',\n@@ -89,7 +92,7 @@ export function resolveMessages(overrides?: Partial<Messages> | null): Messages\n }\n \n export function messageLanguage(messages: Messages, key: keyof Messages): 'en' | null {\n-  return messages[key] === defaultMessages[key] && !authoredMessages.get(messages)?.has(key) ? 'en' : null;\n+  return (messages[key] ?? defaultMessages[key]) === defaultMessages[key] && !authoredMessages.get(messages)?.has(key) ? 'en' : null;\n }\n \n export function fillChartSummary(\ndiff --git a/packages/axylo/src/public.ts b/packages/axylo/src/public.ts\nindex 36a2a53..f34097d 100644\n--- a/packages/axylo/src/public.ts\n+++ b/packages/axylo/src/public.ts\n@@ -205,8 +205,16 @@ export interface Messages {\n   plotRole: string; pointAll: string; seriesValue: string; position: string;\n   /** Label of the stack total in tooltips. */\n   total: string;\n-  /** Single-click panning (WCAG 2.5.7), the table's \"Jump to\" when nothing matches, and how to move in the plot. */\n-  panLeft: string; panRight: string; jumpNotFound: string; plotInstructions: string;\n+  /** Single-click panning (WCAG 2.5.7) and the table's \"Jump to\" when nothing matches. */\n+  panLeft: string; panRight: string; jumpNotFound: string;\n+  /** Point navigation and selection. An override is also the fallback for donuts and receives only explicitly overridden additions. */\n+  plotInstructions: string;\n+  /** Slice navigation and selection, in place of `plotInstructions` on a donut. */\n+  donutInstructions?: string;\n+  /** Added when the arrow keys can move between visible series. */\n+  seriesInstructions?: string;\n+  /** Added when the plot offers Zoom in. */\n+  zoomInstructions?: string;\n   /** Toolbar toggle: while it is on, two clicks in the plot set the two ends of the zoom range (the non-dragging way to select a range, WCAG 2.5.7). */\n   selectRange: string;\n   /** A stack whose components have mixed signs: both ends, in place of one total ('{positive} and {negative}'). */\n| F11 | Line, area and scatter are drawn in x order whatever the input order. On line, area and bar, two rows with the same x in one series are AX108 and that series is not drawn. On scatter, points sharing an x (or both coordinates) are ordinary data. | Shuffled `trend` renders identically; duplicate fixture | R5 |\n| F12 | When a warning means values were left out or changed, the chart says so to the reader: a short note (\"Values not shown: 2. See table.\", worded so it reads correctly for any count) inside the figure and in the accessibility tree, in every build. | Production build given `dirty` shows the note | R5, R6 |\n\n### 3.2 Legibility\n\n| ID | Criterion | Verified by | Driven by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears without the reader being told. Remedies, in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to at most three lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping every label distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. Axylo never changes a chart's orientation on its own. | In a browser, as painted text and not in a model (in the engines of section 2.3 where results are recorded), after fonts load: for widths 240–1,920 px and generated label sets, zero intersecting text boxes (1 px tolerance), zero text outside the figure, truncated labels pairwise distinct. Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides, 200% text-only zoom, and a font that loads late | R2, WCAG 1.4.12, 1.4.4 |\n| L2 | Text is at least 12 CSS px and at least 4.5:1 against what is behind it, including text drawn inside a mark and legend entries for hidden series. Marks, axis lines and focus indicators are at least 3:1. Gridlines are exempt: they are not needed to read a value while the tooltip and table exist. Holds in light and dark. | Computed-style and rendered-pixel checks in both schemes | R7, R10, WCAG 1.4.3, 1.4.11 |\n| L3 | The chart follows its container with no call from the page, in both directions. With no definite height, the plot is 16:9, clamped between 160 and 480 CSS px tall, and the title, controls and table flow above and below it. A container that starts hidden or zero-sized draws when it gets a size. | Resize 720 → 360 → 720 px; hidden-then-shown test; `height: auto` container is stable over 10 frames | R16, D1 |\n| L4 | Light or dark is taken from the chart element's computed `color-scheme`; if that is not set, from the luminance of the inherited text color. `--axylo-background` overrides both. Marks repaint within one frame when the scheme, forced colors, contrast preference, or the `class`, `style` or `data-theme` of `<html>` or `<body>` changes. Forced-colors mode uses system colors. | A page that sets `color-scheme`; a class-toggled dark theme without it; a light-only page on a dark device (must stay light); a runtime toggle; forced-colors emulation | R10 |\n| L5 | A marker on every point appears only when adjacent points are at least 12 px apart (provisional value), and always for isolated points. | `trend` at 720 px has no marker on every point (A5's sparse shape markers remain); a 12-point line has them | R8 |\n| L6 | Title, subtitle and axis titles with units are part of the chart. A value axis is titled with its label (the field name when none is given) and unit. An x axis that is a measure (number) is titled the same way; a time, date or category x axis is titled only when the author gives a `label`, since its ticks already say what it is. A reference line or band shows its label next to it. Axis titles never overlap tick labels. | Layout tests; `trend` fixture | R9, WCAG 2.4.6 |\n| L7 | Empty data shows a message inside the plot area; so do loading, error and Axylo's own internal failures. No invented axis ranges, no blank box. A change of state is announced once, politely. | `empty` fixture: message visible and in the accessibility tree, no tick labels; forced internal error shows the error state | R6, WCAG 4.1.3 |\n| L8 | When the figure cannot hold a readable plot (less than 120×80 CSS px for the plot), it shows the title, a short summary (the first sentence of the generated summary, on at most two lines, cut with an ellipsis beyond that; the full summary remains the figure's description) and the table control instead, and raises AX142. | Narrow and short container tests | R2 |\n\n### 3.3 Interaction\n\n| ID | Criterion | Verified by | Driven by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | Pointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the picking rule for the chart type (section 3.6), within one frame at the 95th percentile. On line, area and bar the tooltip lists every visible series at the nearest x; a series with no row at that x reads \"No observation\", distinct from \"No data\". The tooltip stays inside the viewport, does not cover the active mark or any control, can itself be hovered, and lists at most eight rows plus \"+N more\". In a plot too small for it (decision 0004: narrower than 240 px or shorter than 140 px) the same content appears as text in a strip reserved under the plot; where even the strip would leave the plot under the minimum of L8, pointing highlights the datum without a readout and the values are in the keyboard reading and the table. Escape closes it until the pointer reaches a different datum. | Hover at 20 positions including all four edges; sparse-series fixture; narrow tile with eight series; Escape test | R15, WCAG 1.4.13, 2.4.11 |\n| I2 | Legend entries that show and hide a series are toggle buttons with a pressed state, operable by click, Enter and Space. A donut's legend lists its slices (F8) and has nothing to hide, so its entries are not toggles and this row does not apply to it. | Keyboard and accessibility-tree tests | R12, WCAG 2.5.3, 4.1.2, 2.1.1 |\n| I3 | Zoom on time, date and numeric x axes is reachable four ways: visible Zoom in, Zoom out and Reset buttons that work with single clicks; drag to select a range; `+`, `-`, `0` and Shift+arrows; and pinch when `zoom: 'touch'` is set. The wheel zooms only while the plot has focus, and never when Ctrl or Meta is held, so browser zoom and page scrolling are not intercepted. | Reach a given range by clicks only; by keyboard only; by drag; page scrolls normally with the pointer over an unfocused chart | D7, R12, WCAG 2.5.1, 2.1.1 |\n| I4 | Every interaction works with a single pointer without dragging, and by touch. Every control is at least 24×24 CSS px. A one-finger drag on a chart scrolls the page (on a compact chart too: it takes no pointer input at all, C1). | Touch emulation; size checks | WCAG 2.5.7, 2.5.8, 2.5.1, 2.5.3, 4.1.2, 2.1.1 |\n| I5 | First render is not animated. An update may transition for at most 200 ms. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` nothing transitions, on first render or on update. | After `document.fonts.ready`: first frame equals the frame at 2.5 s within a 0.1% pixel tolerance, in both settings; an update under reduced motion reaches its final frame in one step; a 24-chart filter change settles within 200 ms | R14 |\n| I6 | A chart fed by `append` shows a Pause/Resume control. While paused, new rows are buffered and the view does not move. | Stream test | WCAG 2.2.2 |\n\n### 3.4 Accessibility\n\nTarget: every WCAG 2.2 level AA success criterion that applies to what Axylo renders, as component-level evidence. Conformance of a page is a property of the page and remains the author's.\n\n| ID | Criterion | Verified by | Driven by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Every chart has an accessible name: its `title`, or the heading named by `labelledBy`, or else a generated name (\"Line chart of Sessions by Day\") with AX140 raised in every build. The title's heading level is the author's (`level`), and it can be hidden visually. Every chart has a generated summary: type, series, x range with time zone, y range, each series' minimum, maximum and last value, and any omissions. `description` adds to the summary and never removes the zone or omission statements. Element ids are unique per chart. | Accessibility-tree snapshot for every fixture; a 24-chart page has no duplicate ids; axe `heading-order` | R11, R13, WCAG 1.1.1, 1.3.1, 2.4.6 |\n| A2 | Keyboard: at most two tab stops while the table is closed, the plot and one toolbar with roving focus that holds legend toggles, zoom, pause and the table control. Every point is reachable in order; the series can be switched; the ends can be reached directly; focus can leave the chart. The focus indicator is at least 2 px and 3:1 and is not hidden by the tooltip. The exact keys and roles are fixed after the pattern spike in M1 (section 8). | Forward and reverse traversal in collapsed, zoomed, streaming and table-open states; focus after hiding the focused series; indicator contrast | R12, WCAG 2.1.1, 2.1.2, 2.4.3, 2.4.7, 2.4.11, 1.4.11 |\n| A3 | Moving focus to a point conveys its text (series, x, value with unit, position) through the focused element's value text: the plot is a native range control whose `aria-valuetext` describes the focused point (decision 0001; earlier drafts said \"accessible name or a polite live region\", which the chosen pattern does not use, and A7 forbids announcements for navigation other than this). On touch screen readers, every point is reachable by swiping, or the table is reachable within two gestures. | Accessibility-tree snapshot after each key. No screen-reader rehearsal is part of 1.0 (the owner's decision, 2026-11-18): what a reader actually speaks on NVDA, VoiceOver or TalkBack has not been checked, and the conformance table says so. The script for such a rehearsal is kept in decision 0001 for when one is done. | R12, R13, WCAG 4.1.2 |\n| A4 | \"View as table\" shows the data as an HTML table built from the normalized data when opened: the title as caption, field labels with units as column headers, x values as row headers, values formatted as in F6. It covers the current x range, 100 rows per page, with every row reachable by paging or by jumping to an x value. It sits in a focusable scroll region no taller than the plot, and opening it does not move other charts. | Table content compared with fixture data, including a value near row 900,000 of 1,000,000; a 24-chart page layout test | R13, WCAG 1.3.1, 1.3.2, 3.3.1 |\n| A5 | Series are never distinguished by color alone, in any mode. Each line and area carries a shape marker at its last point and at sparse intervals, repeated in the legend and tooltip; under `prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors, lines also differ by dash. Adjacent filled marks (slices, stacked segments) are separated by at least 1 px of background. Bars are told apart by position and order, and by the legend and tooltip that name them; a compact chart has neither, so there neighbouring bar series also differ by fill pattern (series further apart may share a pattern: four patterns exist). The default palette has eight colors, each at least 3:1 on the default light and dark backgrounds, with a minimum pairwise OKLab difference of 0.10 (provisional) under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia. On any other background, Axylo measures the palette against the resolved background and raises AX141 below 3:1. | Palette script scoring the rendered marks of an eight-series chart in both schemes, repeats included; rendered-pixel checks of separators; a grayscale screenshot in which three crossing lines can be told apart by marker | R7, WCAG 1.4.1, 1.4.11 |\n| A6 | Content reflows at 320 CSS px and 400% zoom without two-dimensional scrolling. User text-spacing overrides do not clip text. | Viewport and style-override tests in three engines | WCAG 1.4.10, 1.4.12 |\n| A7 | Data arriving does not speak. Announcements happen only for the reader's own navigation, and for a change of state (L7). While data streams, keyboard focus stays on the same datum until it leaves the window. | Stream test counting live-region changes with and without focus; 24 concurrent streams | R12 |\n| A8 | axe-core reports no violations on any fixture in any state, including `heading-order` and `scrollable-region-focusable`. | CI | R11 |\n| A9 | A conformance table lists every applicable WCAG 2.2 AA success criterion, the test that covers it, and what the author must supply (a meaningful title or `labelledBy`, series names, units, the page's own structure). It also states the limits in section 3.8. The criteria are the ones cited as \"WCAG x.y.z\" in the last column of this document's criterion rows; a criterion of WCAG 2.2 A or AA that no row cites is listed in the table as not covered by a test, with a word on why: not applicable to a chart component, the page's responsibility, or not assessed (it can apply to a chart, and no test is cited for it; the table claims nothing about it). | Published with each release; a CI check that every listed test exists | R11 |\n| A10 | Every built-in string can be replaced through `messages`. Built-in English text is marked `lang=\"en\"` when the document language is not English. | Test on a `lang=\"de\"` page | WCAG 3.1.2 |\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
